The love for the donut in the United States is longstanding and deep-rooted. Gourmet donut shops have popped up in trendy neighborhoods across the country and high-end restaurants are serving trios of donuts for dessert, while Dunkin' Donuts, Krispy Kreme, and Tim Hortons have amassed a devoted following. In this captivating guide to the delectable dessert, culinary historian, chef, and donut lover Michael Krondl has put together an entertaining social history of the donut throughout the ages and from around the world. Among the interesting facts Krondl brings up are the donut's surprising role, not only as a traditional prelude to Lent, but in Hanukkah and Ramadan as well; the serving of donuts to American doughboys in the trenches of World War I; and the delivery by Red Cross Clubmobiles of essential comforts of home to World War II soldiers such as music, movies, magazines and--what else?--donut machines. Mindful that the information might have readers itching to run to their nearest bakery, Krondl also offers a baker's dozen of international donut recipes--with accompanying color photos--including those for Chocolate-Glazed Bismarcks with Marshmallow Filling, Nutella Bombolocini, Frittelle di Carnevale, and Dulce de Leche Raised Donuts with a Salty Caramel Glaze, among others."�
�"... tova e istoriia,v koiato mozhesh da ogledash sebe si,napisana na ezik,koito da pripoznaesh,s's zapomniashchi se obrazi,koito da zaobichash,za da se v'rnesh obratno i da ia prochetesh oshche vedn'zh,kakto se preprochitat liubimi knigi. Vazhen za b'lgarskata literatura roman. "
Silviia Choleva, Literaturen vestnik
"... P'rviiat roman na Teodora Dimova ,dosega izvestna edinstveno kato avtorka na piesi,oshche na pr'v pogled obeshchava da b'de s'bite v nai-novata ni literatura. "
Milena Kirova,
v-k KULTURA
"... EMINE ima zrial romanov stil. Negovata analitichna vgl'benost,liriz'm i patos otpraviat s'm edno zhensko Az,koeto m'chitelno uznava s'shchnostta si na fatalna zhena /ili po-tochno na zhena-fatum/ obrechena da presicha vremena, prostranstva, m'zhe... Tova e kniga za nevedomoto u nas, za chuplivostta i ustoichivostta ni. Kniga za razdvoiavaneto, chrez koeto postigame edinstvoto si. "
Plamen Antov, v-k KAPITAL
"... V EMINE potok't ot uverenost v izmisleniia sviat i ot s'mneniia k'm stavashchoto naokolo se otticha v siakash bezkraini izrecheniia, s rit'ma na vdishvaneto i izdishvaneto,s'sredotocheno,vnimatelno i delikatno,kato che li izbiagvaiki da stigne tochkata,za de ne prek'sne niakak'v zhivot. "
v-k "Standart"
"Iana Ilinda - taka Teodora Dimova e kr'stila geroiniata na debiutniia si roman EMINE. Ako povtorish imeto niakolko p'ti,melodiiata mu otnachalo shche te zamae, a posle shche te uspokoi,vse edno,che izrichash mantra. Tochno taka deistva vsiaka prelistena stranitsa ot knigata na Dimova. Uvlicha te vse poveche i poveche,dokato stignesh zad'khan do posledniia list.... "
Elena Kr'steva, v-k MONITOR
"Spored knigorazprostranitelite EMINE e khitovo zaglavie na pazara. V tozi fakt niama nishcho uchudvashcho,zashchoto Teodora Dimova e veche utv'rdeno ime v b'lgarskata dramaturgiia. "
v-k DNEVNIK
"Chuite tezi imena: Iana Ilinda,Silian,Mina... I tova stiga,za da usetim spetsifichnata ezichesko - pravoslavna mistika na EMINE,p'rviiat roman na Teodora Dimova. Nalozhila se kato dramaturg /Igrila, Stop'r i dr/ avtorkata obiasniava,che roman't i e nerealizirana piesa,koiato uporito t'rsela svoiata forma. Veroiatno ekstremnata chuvstvitelnost na geroite ne e mogla da se zatvori v dialozi iramki; preliala e v nagneteniia,uvlichashch potok na s'znanieto v EMINE. "
Biliana Kurtasheva, sp. EGOIST"�
�Cled pomana "Alkokhol", v koito se pazkazva za d'noto na zhivota, a sled tova i za v'zkhoda i spasenieto, v "Ludost" Kalin Tepziiski se vpuska v padenieto nadolu i biagstvoto nav'n. Chetipite godini v psikhiatpichna bolnitsa - kato lekap, no i kato vliuben, kato bopets speshchu bezsmislieto i t'psach na smis'la - tova e temata na pazkaza, koito izp'lva v'lnuvashchite stpanitsi na pomana "Ludost".
"Mitove ili deistvitelnost. Ili deistvitelnost i mitove. Kalin Terziiski poema tpudniia, tp'nliv i stp'men p't na sebepoznanieto na p'ba na pochti fotogpafski obpazi. Pesimizm't i nikhilizm't ne mogat da ppikpiiat d'lbokiia stpemezh na avtopa za s'shchestvuvane v edin sviat na pomantichnost. Ppozipashchiiat na fona na mpachnite kaptini optimiz'm ni vodi do obobshcheniia, ot koito dnes vsichki se nuzhdaem."
D-p Ivan Gepdzhikov
"Lekuvashch psikhiat'p ili popedni patsient v ludnitsata na sveta? Ludostta na Kalin Tepziiski e zapazitelna"
Zakhari Karabashliev"�
�The greatest French poet of the 19th century, Baudelaire was also the first truly modem poet, and his direct and indirect influence on the literature of our time has been immeasurable.
Flowers of Evil: A Selectioncontains 53 poems which the editors feel best represent the total work and which. in their opinion, have been most successfully rendered into English. The French texts as established by Yves Gerard Le Dantec for the Pleiade edition are printed en face. Included are Baudelaire's "Three Drafts of a Preface" and brief notes on the nineteen translators whose work is represented."�
�V edin top'l oktomvriiski den izt'knatiiat portlandski advokat Dzherald B'rlingeim i s'prugata mu Dzhesi otivat v liatnata si k'shcha do ezeroto Kashuakamak. Dzherald e planiral uikend, v koito shche os'shchestvi niakoi ot po-neobichainite si seksualni fantazii. Toi zakopchava Dzhesi s beleznitsi za legloto, no tozi p't tia otkazva da uchastva v igrata. Ot otegchitelna situatsiiata za neia prerastva v koshmar, zashchoto Dzherald poluchava infarkt i tia ostava prikovana za legloto v praznata k'shcha na pustiia ezeren briag.
Tova, koeto sledva, mozhe da b'de opisano edinstveno ot Stiv'n King.
Okovana i bezpomoshchna, Dzhesi pot'va v nai-m'chitelnata ,,cherna noshch na dushata". Reshena da zapazi razs'd'ka si i da se osvobodi, tia minava prez ada na sobstvenite si spomeni i prez nai- uzhasnite si strakhove, zashchoto v k'shchata se prom'kva ozverialo ot glad kuche, a noshchem ot t'mniia 'g'l na spalniata ia nabliudava zloveshch, siakash izliaz'l ot preizpodniata nepoznat."�
